        en: 'Until this very moment your program was a respectful reader: it opened files, read them, and changed not a letter. Today it gets a pen: mode \'w\' opens a file for writing — and if the file already exists, its old content is wiped before the first character you write. Power and danger in one letter. By the end of this lesson you will be able to: open a file in write mode, know what write() returns, and close the cycle by closing the file and re-reading it to verify.',
