          en: "To write a file you must open it in mode 'w' as the second argument: out = open('output.txt', 'w'). The default mode was reading 'r'; writing 'w' creates the file if it does not exist — and the big trap: if the file already exists, its old content is wiped entirely and an empty file opens. Whole programs have lost their data to this small letter.",
